  "verbalization": "Notoamide B is implicated in the interaction with NH-6 through a series of molecular targets, with the most direct link being its targeting of Malme-3M, which in turn is targeted by Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-. This pathway suggests that Notoamide B may act through a shared mechanism with Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, ultimately leading to the activation of NH-6. The evidence from the three paths indicates a potential convergent pathway where Notoamide B and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)- both target Malme-3M and then NH-6, suggesting a possible functional overlap or a common downstream effect. The scores from the paths support a strong association between Notoamide B and NH-6, but the exact mechanism by which Notoamide B influences NH-6 remains to be elucidated. The integration of these findings highlights a potential role for Notoamide B in modulating the activity of NH-6 through a multi-targeted pathway.",
